{
  "card": "Jace, Reality Sculptor",
  "title": "the [0] ignores its twenty-five-loyalty activation restriction",
  "status": "active",
  "kind": "parser",
  "upstream_issue": null,
  "marks_supported": true,
  "applies_to": {
    "server_version": "0.117.0",
    "build_commit": "09c286c",
    "card_data_sha256": "84d5fd2af84e2f125b740eeb05637785b2e8df26d34e41a2cd628697dae30513",
    "entry_sha256": "fe97cbc2a151e2e65163e2c16c8a38979748972a59df7bc051e7979004852bc3"
  },
  "rules": {
    "oracle": "[+1]: Empower Jace X, where X is the number of Islands you control.\n[−3]: Until your next turn, whenever a creature attacks you or a planeswalker you control, it gets -5/-0 until end of turn.\n[0]: Exile all but the bottom card of each opponent's library. Activate only if there are twenty-five or more loyalty counters among Jaces you control.",
    "cr": [
      "602.5b",
      "606.3",
      "701.71a",
      "611.2b",
      "603.7a"
    ],
    "actual": "The [0] can be activated whatever the number of loyalty counters: with fewer than twenty-five among the Jaces you control it is still offered, and it exiles all but the bottom card of each opponent's library. Opponents' Jaces aren't the issue; there is simply no restriction. [+1] and [−3] are correct.",
    "expected": "\"Activate only if there are twenty-five or more loyalty counters among Jaces you control\" restricts when the [0] can be activated (CR 602.5b): it counts the loyalty counters on every Jace permanent you control (Jace, Reality Sculptor itself, Jace planeswalker tokens and other Jaces), not your opponents' Jaces, and is checked only as you activate (the [0] cost doesn't change the count). Below twenty-five the ability can't be activated at all; at twenty-five or more it resolves and exiles all but the bottom card of each opponent's library. The usual loyalty timing still applies (sorcery speed, once per turn per planeswalker, CR 606.3).",
    "diagnosis": "The parser attaches the correct threshold (QuantityCheck: CountersOnObjects{loyalty, Jaces you control} >= 25) as the condition of a sub_ability whose effect is Unimplemented{unrecognized_clause_head: \"Activate only\"}, i.e. the restriction sentence is treated as one more effect step. The Unimplemented step is a no-op, and activation_restrictions keeps only AsSorcery, so nothing gates activation.",
    "suggested_fix": "When a loyalty ability line ends with \"Activate only if <condition>.\", have the activated-ability parser lower it to ActivationRestriction::RequiresCondition{condition: ParsedCondition::QuantityComparison{lhs: Ref(CountersOnObjects{counter_type: loyalty, filter: Typed{[Subtype Jace], controller: You}}), comparator: GE, rhs: Fixed 25}} appended to activation_restrictions (after AsSorcery), the same restriction shape non-loyalty \"Activate only if you control three or more artifacts\" (Argent Sphinx) produces, instead of splitting it into an Unimplemented \"Activate only\" sub_ability. can_activate_loyalty_ability_impl already evaluates activation_restrictions for loyalty abilities, so no engine change is needed.",
    "override_note": "The patch drops the Unimplemented sub-step and appends RequiresCondition{QuantityComparison(CountersOnObjects{loyalty, Typed{Subtype Jace, controller You}} >= 25)} to the [0]'s activation_restrictions. Loyalty abilities go through the shared activation-restriction check (legal actions and the activation handler alike), which evaluates the comparison from the activating player's side when the ability is activated (CR 602.5b): loyalty counters on all battlefield Jaces you control are summed, opponents' Jaces aren't. The [0]'s effect (ExileTop of each opponent's library, count = that library's size - 1) and the [+1] and [−3] are unchanged and were tested as guards."
  },
  "patch": [
    {
      "op": "test",
      "path": "/abilities/2/cost",
      "value": {
        "type": "Loyalty",
        "amount": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "test",
      "path": "/abilities/2/effect/type",
      "value": "ExileTop"
    },
    {
      "op": "test",
      "path": "/abilities/2/sub_ability/effect",
      "value": {
        "type": "Unimplemented",
        "name": "unrecognized_clause_head",
        "description": "Activate only"
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "test",
      "path": "/abilities/2/sub_ability/condition",
      "value": {
        "type": "QuantityCheck",
        "lhs": {
          "type": "Ref",
          "qty": {
            "type": "CountersOnObjects",
            "counter_type": "loyalty",
            "filter": {
              "type": "Typed",
              "type_filters": [
                {
                  "Subtype": "Jace"
                }
              ],
              "controller": "You",
              "properties": []
            }
          }
        },
        "comparator": "GE",
        "rhs": {
          "type": "Fixed",
          "value": 25
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "test",
      "path": "/abilities/2/activation_restrictions",
      "value": [
        {
          "type": "AsSorcery"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/abilities/2/sub_ability",
      "value": null
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/abilities/2/activation_restrictions/-",
      "value": {
        "type": "RequiresCondition",
        "data": {
          "condition": {
            "type": "QuantityComparison",
            "lhs": {
              "type": "Ref",
              "qty": {
                "type": "CountersOnObjects",
                "counter_type": "loyalty",
                "filter": {
                  "type": "Typed",
                  "type_filters": [
                    {
                      "Subtype": "Jace"
                    }
                  ],
                  "controller": "You",
                  "properties": []
                }
              }
            },
            "comparator": "GE",
            "rhs": {
              "type": "Fixed",
              "value": 25
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  ],
